From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PickleHik3 <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wi-Fi and mobile managers: from the launcher's network events

With -Dlauncherctl, wifi-manager-tl.c (PhoshWifiManager) and PhoshWWanTl (the PhoshWWan
implementation the shell picks) show the watch stream's network event: Wi-Fi on or off,
connected, SSID, signal level 0 to 4 as the usual signal icons; cellular present, signal level,
network type as 2G to 5G, mobile data on or off for the no-data icons. Both only show: they
cannot switch Wi-Fi, scan, connect, switch the radio or mobile data. Without a launcher both are
not present, like the managers of a build without a backend, and their tiles stay insensitive.

wwan-manager-none.c's get_data_enabled and has_data now ask the object's property, which is
FALSE for the base class and the launcher's value for PhoshWWanTl, which overrides it.

diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
index 4795073..b1b66a0 100644
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -472,6 +472,9 @@ if have_networkmanager
     'network-auth-manager.c',
     'network-auth-prompt.c',
   )
+elif have_launcherctl
+  # Wi-Fi without NetworkManager, from the launcher
+  phosh_tool_sources += files('wifi-manager-tl.c')
 else
   # Wi-Fi without NetworkManager: a manager that has no hardware to report
   phosh_tool_sources += files('wifi-manager-none.c')
